{"version":1,"id":"M4L.dl.transposer~","preview":{"id":"M4L.dl.transposer~","objectName":"M4L.dl.transposer~","helpFilePath":"max://C74/patchers/m4l/Lessons resources/M4L.dl.transposer~.maxpat","renderMode":"top-level-fallback","patcherRect":[25,69,485,442],"boxes":[{"id":"obj-44","maxclass":"comment","text":"Note: the gizmo~ object must be used inside a pfft~ with an window overlap of 4 or more - using an overlap of 2 will produce an audible amount of amplitude modulation. The gizmo~ object won't do anything if you try to use it outside of a pfft~ object.","rect":[16,376,427,44],"patchingRect":[16,376,427,44],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial Italic","fontsize":11,"linecount":3},{"id":"obj-43","maxclass":"comment","text":"<","rect":[157,96,19,18],"patchingRect":[157,96,19,18],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":10},{"id":"obj-42","maxclass":"comment","text":"<","rect":[156,344,19,18],"patchingRect":[156,344,19,18],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":10},{"id":"obj-41","maxclass":"comment","text":"When we're done, we perform an Inverse Fast Fourier Transform to translate the signal back into the time domain and output the resulting audio signal.","rect":[168,320,250,41],"patchingRect":[168,320,250,41],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":10,"linecount":3},{"id":"obj-40","maxclass":"comment","text":"Spectral transposer","rect":[40,300,64,29],"patchingRect":[40,300,64,29],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial Bold","fontsize":10,"linecount":2,"textcolor":[0.3,0.34,0.4,1]},{"id":"obj-39","maxclass":"comment","text":"Translate the signal from the  time domain into the frequency domain by performing a windowed Fast Fourier Transform.","rect":[168,84,199,41],"patchingRect":[168,84,199,41],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":10,"linecount":3},{"id":"obj-38","maxclass":"comment","text":"Input signal","rect":[32,96,67,18],"patchingRect":[32,96,67,18],"numinlets":1